      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I understand the test. It calls `WordUtils.wrap()` with a negative `wrapLength`, a custom `newLineStr`, and a custom `wrapOn` regex—all using the same cryptic string literal. Let me improve the understandability by naming variables meaningfully and extracting the repeated literal into a constant.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version extracts the repeated string literal into a named constant `SHARED_TOKEN`, renames the result variable from `string0` to `wrappedResult`, and adds a comment explaining the non-obvious behavior (negative `wrapLength` clamped to 1, and the dual role of the token as both the wrap-on regex and newline separator)."
